text → `[{\"word\":\"a\",\"count\":1},{\"word\":\"ab\",\"count\":1},{\"word\":\"abc\",\"count\":1},{\"word\":\"été\",\"count\":1}]`. json.Marshal escapes non-ASCII? Go's encoding/json escapes HTML characters (<,>,&) but not non-ASCII letters — it outputs UTF-8 as-is. Yes, only U+2028/U+2029 escaped. So \"été\" stays literal.\n\nJSON with empty input → `[]`.\n\nJSON with min-length filter → `[{\"word\":\"abc\",\"count\":1},{\"word\":\"été\",\"count\":1}]`.\n\nErrors: \"-min-length 0\" → stderr \"wordstat: -min-length must be 1 or more\\n\", code 2, stdout empty. \"-min-length -1\" same. \"-format xml\" → \"wordstat: -format must be text or json\\n\" code 2.\n\nAlso test files: args with file path, stdin ignored. e.g. args [\"-min-length\",\"3\",file] → same output.\n\nTable-driven with fields args, stdin, wantStdout, wantStderr, wantCode.\n\nAlso test that both flags work together with file and stdin.\n\nLet me write a single comprehensive table test plus separate file-based test.\n\nAlso verify -min-length counts characters not bytes: \"été\" length 3 → with -min-length 3 included; -min-length 4 excluded.\n\nApostrophes: \"don't\" length 5.\n\nLet me write the test file.\n\nNote: for file test with args, flags.NArg() == 0 → stdin not read. Good.\n\nLet me create main_test.go.\n\nAlso add count package test for AddWithMinLength? The task says add table-driven tests for the new flags, go test ./... . I'll add a table test in count_test.go for AddWithMinLength too — good coverage.\n\nLet me write main_test.go.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e618250a001Xox0WZ1g1KQ0ij","sessionID":"ses_e19e95074ffegU8hqosXpy99ES","messageID":"msg_1e617906b001FQUXJ45cA8JfgO"}}
