capes non-ASCII? No, it keeps UTF-8 as-is (only escapes <, >, &, and U+2028/2029). Good — \"été\" appears literally.\n\nLet me verify exit code with a built binary.\n\nAlso should update README to document new flags. The task says \"Everything else stays as it is\" — but documenting new flags in README is reasonable and helpful. Let me add brief docs.\n\nLet me also double check: `-min-length` with a value like \"abc\" (non-numeric) → flag parse error → exit 2 with flag package error message. That's fine.\n\nAlso check `-format` given but empty string handled.\n\nOne more: the spec says \"-min-length N skips words shorter than N characters (letters, digits and apostrophes; count characters, not bytes)\". My implementation counts runes of the whole word. Words consist only of letters/digits/apostrophes already after trimming. Good.\n\nEdge: word \"don't\" — apostrophe counts as a character → length 5. Good.\n\nNow verify exit codes with built binary.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e61936b80017BsN75MKk1DUeq","sessionID":"ses_e19e95074ffegU8hqosXpy99ES","messageID":"msg_1e618e869001Dy8qy5DL9q9Tcq"}}
