{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794861788234,"sessionID":"ses_e19e95074ffegU8hqosXpy99ES","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_99c05eccbd1d449a872c4444","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/go-cli-feature/opencode-1/repo/README.md","newString":"```bash\ngo run . -top 5 notes.txt more.txt   # the five most frequent words over both files\ngo run . < notes.txt                 # read standard input; default -top 10\ngo run . -min-length 4 notes.txt     # ignore words shorter than four characters\ngo run . -format json notes.txt      # one JSON array instead of text lines\ngo test ./...\n```\n\nA word is a run of letters, digits and apostrophes, compared in lower case. Output is one\n`count<TAB>word` line per word, most frequent first, ties in alphabetical order. Errors go to\nstandard error as `wordstat: <message>` with exit status 2 (bad flags) or 1 (unreadable file).\n\n## Flags\n\n- `-top N` how many words to print, `0` for all (default `10`).\n- `-min-length N` skip words shorter than `N` characters (default `1`, counts every word).\n  Characters, not bytes, are counted, so `été` has length 3. `-top` applies after the filter.\n- `-format text|json` output format (default `text`). `json` prints a single line holding a JSON\n  array of `{\"word\": \"...\", \"count\": N}` objects in the same order as the text output, or `[]`\n  when there are no words.","oldString":"```bash\ngo run . -top 5 notes.txt more.txt   # the five most frequent words over both files\ngo run . < notes.txt                 # read standard input; default -top 10\ngo test ./...\n```\n\nA word is a run of letters, digits and apostrophes, compared in lower case. Output is one\n`count<TAB>word` line per word, most frequent first, ties in alphabetical order. Errors go to\nstandard error as `wordstat: <message>` with exit status 2 (ba